# Visible Exterior Book Tabs and Larger Reading Text

Status: DONE
Milestone: M30 Correct the visible book silhouette and reading scale
Dependencies: 24_LARGER_EDGE_BOOK_TABS.todo; 34_EXTRA_PALE_PINK_COVERS.todo

## Purpose

The owner reiterated that open-book tabs must protrude visibly, not remain inside
the outer rounded panel. They like the closed-cover flags but reject the visible
inner attachment rectangles, and want larger reading/action text inside books.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve current notebook CSS, behavior, markup, tests and context.
- [x] Identify the opaque outer dialog/gutter as a visible-envelope issue missed
  by earlier internal-paper edge measurements.
- [x] Paint closed-cover flags only outside the pink paper, hiding their attachment.
- [x] Move open-book actions beyond the visible paper outline with clear photo association.
- [x] Remove the surrounding filled dialog panel that visually encloses the tabs.
- [x] Increase inside reading/labels while preserving large actual click/tap targets.
- [x] Retain four photos, contained imagery, no modal scrolling and honest static fallback.
- [x] Check actual inner-cover pixels, outer silhouettes, focus and enlarged-text layouts.
- [x] Refresh current campaign images and publish only scoped notebook changes.

## Acceptance criteria

- No coloured attachment rectangle visible over the closed pink cover.
- Actual open-book outline ends before the exposed tabs; native logical gutters
  remain transparent and do not visually absorb the tags.
- Essential inside text is at least18px, with visibly larger captions/headings;
  no shrinking text to pass a former fitting threshold.
- Correct photo/enquiry associations, keyboard/focus return,48pxtargets and safe
  no-JS/module/style/reduced-motion fallbacks remain.
- Four photos per page remain; extreme readable-text cases may use the complete
  static view, never clipped content or secretly fewer-photo pages.
- No image-tool views or automatic inference of owner aesthetic acceptance.

